# The Dock icon's menu lists each window Cra shows, once. With one browser window it listed the page twice: Chrome's
# window that holds a profile's pages is never seen (alpha 0, bridge.mm) but stays ordered in, titled after its
# active tab, so AppKit put it in the Window menu and the Dock menu read it from there (Victor, 20 Nov); hidden
# DevTools added a third row. Chrome's hidden windows are left out of the Window menu now (NeverKeyOrMain); on
# engine -2 the first readout is `2 [main, "Fixture main" hidden docked]`.
budget rss=900
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=main
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 2
cra://debug?windowsMenu=page
expect-log windows menu page: 1 \[main\]

# A second tab: still one window.
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=second
wait 2
cra://debug?windowsMenu=tabs
expect-log windows menu tabs: 1 \[main\]

# DevTools docked beside the page: Chrome's DevTools window is hidden too.
cra://action/devTools
wait 4
cra://debug?windowsMenu=devtools
expect-log windows menu devtools: 1 \[main\]
cra://action/devTools
wait 3

# A Little Window's page is a hidden Chrome window too.
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=little
wait 3
cra://debug?windowsMenu=little
expect-log windows menu little: .*main
reject-log windows menu .*(hidden|docked)
reject-log fault:
